<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-all</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:07:32Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-all" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-all" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Indian workers fill Germany's labor gaps but face hurdles and risks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c8298db7818baea25859c4dbde27fd437f177cfd045c1444ec1ac66813cea133</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-28T06:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/indian-workers-fill-germany-s-labor-gaps-but-face-hurdles-and-risks/a-80072882--78ecce9504e7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/indian-workers-fill-germany-s-labor-gaps-but-face-hurdles-and-risks/a-80072882?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The number of Indians working in Germany has grown rapidly in recent years. But many continue to face challenges in the labor market. Some also fall victim to recruitment scams, leaving them vulnerable to exploitation.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Polls open in Taiwan's closely watched local elections</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1d649a408fd5fa1e3b32500dfa584816e5b2992ff372d59cf7904aedac73429d</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:07:09Z</updated><published>2026-11-28T02:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/polls-open-in-taiwan-s-closely-watched-local-elections/a-80083086--10a314bcb067.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/polls-open-in-taiwan-s-closely-watched-local-elections/a-80083086?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Polls have opened for local elections in Taiwan. While campaigners have stayed away from the topic of China and focused on issues like transport and childcare, Beijing has repeatedly weighed in.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Spain's Sanchez makes final appeal to voters before election</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bcc8b44a12542269f75a96773274420574922cbee81b26beb84309bbbf015ec2</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:07:12Z</updated><published>2026-11-28T00:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/spain-s-sanchez-makes-final-appeal-to-voters-before-election/a-80082783--097c77a9a9e9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/spain-s-sanchez-makes-final-appeal-to-voters-before-election/a-80082783?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Spanish Prime Minister Pedro Sanchez told people to turn out in large numbers so the country does not go "backwards." Polls suggest an end to his eight-year leftist leadership of Spain.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>US disables ship in Gulf of Oman under Iran blockade</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:68a52a8ccfa2eae96381fa4230c71bcf583a359011e2a42ed3a0247e2afbe1ad</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:07:14Z</updated><published>2026-11-27T23:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-disables-ship-in-gulf-of-oman-under-iran-blockade/a-80082950--319498537e26.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-disables-ship-in-gulf-of-oman-under-iran-blockade/a-80082950?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The United States said it was continuing "to strictly enforce the blockade" of Iran's ports. Meanwhile, Kuwait summoned Iran's ambassador over a strike that killed two Italian technicians.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Canada: Supreme Court largely upholds Quebec secularism bill</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3db8de2173c7c06e62a7389117fb4369785f091e420c7e8f57ba6997d0811086</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:07:17Z</updated><published>2026-11-27T20:43:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/canada-supreme-court-largely-upholds-quebec-secularism-bill/a-80082571--e81b43653220.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/canada-supreme-court-largely-upholds-quebec-secularism-bill/a-80082571?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Quebec's government passed Bill 21 to ban religious symbols for public servants, arguing it was necessary to protect its secularist society. Critics argue the bill weakens legal protections for fundamental rights.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Lawmakers approve debt-laden 2027 budget</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:368029654d3d398799eec8bb65a7fa2cead9123e5e3c6d8d1b5eba116ab363bd</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:07:20Z</updated><published>2026-11-27T19:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-lawmakers-approve-debt-laden-2027-budget/live-80071074--c798e4fa7b92.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-lawmakers-approve-debt-laden-2027-budget/live-80071074?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">German lawmakers voted on a federal budget which foresees €556 billion in spending. Elsewhere, the Left Party is hosting a summit on femicide and the BSW party conference starts in Dresden. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Spanish rider Marc Marquez announces MotoGP retirement, days after clinching record 8th world title</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:39e3345a10f0cbdb5d84e3e6da8aabdb40153e7ba7fa641cb622b7fe22cf5178</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-27T18:01:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/spanish-rider-marc-marquez-announces-motogp-retirement-days-after-clinching-record-8th-world-title/a-80079930--3f20c4c08f5b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/spanish-rider-marc-marquez-announces-motogp-retirement-days-after-clinching-record-8th-world-title/a-80079930?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Marc Marquez took fans and his team by surprise when announcing this weekend's race in Valencia will be his last. The 33-year-old won a record eight MotoGP titles, including his rookie and retirement seasons.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>France seeks German man in Channel migrant boat probe</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a722b6d027b87a734d4860c7ede05f6adcbd52cc5dabb38ca854c67274300497</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-27T16:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/france-seeks-german-man-in-channel-migrant-boat-probe/a-80078069--841769bf9248.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/france-seeks-german-man-in-channel-migrant-boat-probe/a-80078069?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A German businessman is accused of supplying equipment to smugglers organizing migrant crossings from France to the United Kingdom. However, he can't face formal charges until he is extradited to France.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Divisions deepen between EU member states after tense budget summit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:90e5491412357425de5be5e5c40bd95e552075586044881e361b91322e1e6390</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-27T16:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/divisions-deepen-between-eu-member-states-after-tense-budget-summit/a-80078599--05a844bfc611.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/divisions-deepen-between-eu-member-states-after-tense-budget-summit/a-80078599?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">An EU leaders summit on the bloc's seven-year budget fell apart amid divisions over how to fund Ukraine. The budget proposal also includes a 3% tax on US tech companies, in a bid for the EU to generate additional funds.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Kanal-Centre Pompidou, Brussels' most anticipated new art museum, opens its doors</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c498480ca048cd9d016e510608337d80bfecc85de357afd6eece72512d4974b8</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:07:23Z</updated><published>2026-11-27T16:15:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/kanal-centre-pompidou-brussels-most-anticipated-new-art-museum-opens-its-doors/a-80001444--f96ce33fc4a2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/kanal-centre-pompidou-brussels-most-anticipated-new-art-museum-opens-its-doors/a-80001444?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A major addition to Europe's cultural scene: Kanal-Centre Pompidou, the new contemporary art museum in a former Citroen factory complex, is celebrating its opening with a free, nonstop weekend program.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Serbia's Student List runs chemistry professor Radomir Saicic for president</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:eede529c32cdb7ce091dd6fddf72896c1c7058247df4b9895480012d91633fe7</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-27T16:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/serbia-s-student-list-runs-chemistry-professor-radomir-saicic-for-president/a-80078700--106ebec53e85.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/serbia-s-student-list-runs-chemistry-professor-radomir-saicic-for-president/a-80078700?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After ousting strongman Aleksandar Vucic, Serbia's student movement has now nominated academic Radomir Saicic for the upcoming presidential vote. Saicic accused the "outgoing regime" of trying to collapse the state.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Dutch authorities seize 26 critically endangered turtles from luggage of passenger bound for Hong Kong</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3c6e456beb77ed2c49f7d01071936f0e5ea4b979632567c9b7ce9109edcc6f0f</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-27T15:48:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/dutch-authorities-seize-26-critically-endangered-turtles-from-luggage-of-passenger-bound-for-hong-ko/a-80077824--bdef9f0677e0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/dutch-authorities-seize-26-critically-endangered-turtles-from-luggage-of-passenger-bound-for-hong-kong/a-80077824?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The tiny Vallarta mud turtle was only discovered in 2018. It's critically endangered with around 300 thought to live in the wild. Almost one tenth of that number were stashed in a traveler's luggage, bound in duct tape.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Arsenic in the water: Thailand presses Myanmar over mining pollution</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6cf5ca0dc637073f1076e2130eb747c5efc11c0423323d5cb3384b39fc1279cc</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-27T14:56:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/arsenic-in-the-water-thailand-presses-myanmar-over-mining-pollution/a-80074295--98cdabbb5354.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/arsenic-in-the-water-thailand-presses-myanmar-over-mining-pollution/a-80074295?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Thailand is seeking to tackle river pollution stemming from rare earth mines in neighboring Myanmar. The two countries held joint talks this week as a "first step towards agreeing on the evidence."</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Georgia: Police clash with Besiktas fans at Israel club game</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d74a6982e195b413185776258e51e4bdc412fbbe631d36b42e90304cc999e302</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-27T14:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/georgia-police-clash-with-besiktas-fans-at-israel-club-game/a-80076111--302857b88ba0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/georgia-police-clash-with-besiktas-fans-at-israel-club-game/a-80076111?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Turkey's Besiktas accused Georgian police of using "disproportionate" force during the game with Israel's Hapoel Beer-Sheva, which saw Besiktas fans unfurl a banner supporting Palestine.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Airline Norse Atlantic files for bankruptcy, succumbing to aviation fuel costs</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7ed458f7cba49bc5609fddf5bfe72e300fa87b8e4063b68ab5a19b43a9dd0943</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-27T14:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/airline-norse-atlantic-files-for-bankruptcy-succumbing-to-aviation-fuel-costs/a-80076728--deb84ffc1870.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/airline-norse-atlantic-files-for-bankruptcy-succumbing-to-aviation-fuel-costs/a-80076728?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The low-cost airline was only founded a few years ago and had been struggling to turn a profit. The spike in aviation fuel prices caused by the war in Iran has now driven Norway's Norse Atlantic into bankruptcy.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>As Gambia gears up for election, can Barrow secure a third term?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f836fa40aa0ad332ae79c7dd8bcb18fe68470e79772252283785926d13679567</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-27T13:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/as-gambia-gears-up-for-election-can-barrow-secure-a-third-term/a-80076340--b6856a8ea5b6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/as-gambia-gears-up-for-election-can-barrow-secure-a-third-term/a-80076340?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">President Adama Barrow is seeking a third term as Gambians vote on December 5. The election will test the opposition's appeal and the country's progress on democratic reform.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Informer TV owner Vucicevic arrested: Has the reckoning with Serbia's pro-Vucic media machine begun?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9d14532cbe34bf13e574abfa1c2b6907269a3197adc43da041757506c5722e4d</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:07:26Z</updated><published>2026-11-27T13:28:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/informer-tv-owner-vucicevic-arrested-has-the-reckoning-with-serbia-s-pro-vucic-media-machine-begun/a-80074650--983ff7ae64ee.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/informer-tv-owner-vucicevic-arrested-has-the-reckoning-with-serbia-s-pro-vucic-media-machine-begun/a-80074650?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The arrest of media owner Dragan J. Vucicevic raises questions about whether Serbia is holding the people behind the country's pro-Vucic media accountable — or whether this is another political power struggle.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Duterte's ICC trial: What is at stake for the Philippines?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b630b154bd320a8d85983e1218eaf5629836e8b98320b4d2a947d7c44315e364</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-27T13:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/duterte-s-icc-trial-what-is-at-stake-for-the-philippines/a-80075657--9d6c676a2419.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/duterte-s-icc-trial-what-is-at-stake-for-the-philippines/a-80075657?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Former Philippine President Rodrigo Duterte faces trial in The Hague over his deadly war on drugs. The proceedings could determine the political fortunes of a powerful dynasty. Victims' families hope to see justice.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>In Iran, child marriage risks complicated by war</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3faa427d6bd21ae08aaace0a27856d1b675297d36077306586df4600af95fa88</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-27T13:06:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/in-iran-child-marriage-risks-complicated-by-war/a-80075473--2a4ac067a146.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/in-iran-child-marriage-risks-complicated-by-war/a-80075473?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">War, poverty and disrupted schooling could put more girls in Iran at risk of child marriage, rights advocates have warned.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Philippines: VP Duterte says father's ICC case 'not a fair trial'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:93fb07d4de9418cecaa27fbc7df2ef0890bd344f19a93f12d23d33413f6eecce</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-27T12:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/philippines-vp-duterte-says-father-s-icc-case-not-a-fair-trial/a-80074359--fe3a5d80492d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/philippines-vp-duterte-says-father-s-icc-case-not-a-fair-trial/a-80074359?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Sara Duterte has said the ICC will not give her father a fair trial and that the Hague-based court wants to "make a statement." Duterte alleges the case against her father is politically motivated.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>The tiny BSW is a party in crisis, as it is set to hand the far-right AfD power in eastern Germany</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6684a1970dc27f7c2f2cf7dd144594cff616600b1501139c069d7a7341612088</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-27T12:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/the-tiny-bsw-is-a-party-in-crisis-as-it-is-set-to-hand-the-far-right-afd-power-in-eastern-germany/a-80074417--98b542aa0047.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/the-tiny-bsw-is-a-party-in-crisis-as-it-is-set-to-hand-the-far-right-afd-power-in-eastern-germany/a-80074417?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Sahra Wagenknecht's BSW party is set to disrupt German politics yet again. Espousing a mix of left-wing economic policy and populist far-right anti-migration rhetoric, it now stands to play kingmaker to the far right AfD</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Russia sports ban: Ukraine's Heraskevych hails EU pushback</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5b8775c3315fe6dff9911d85b62644809306e12d47c3070d31efb69d8c09c72f</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:07:30Z</updated><published>2026-11-27T12:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russia-sports-ban-ukraine-s-heraskevych-hails-eu-pushback/a-80074375--fdb750d9b0f2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russia-sports-ban-ukraine-s-heraskevych-hails-eu-pushback/a-80074375?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As European countries challenge Russia's sporting return, Ukrainian Olympian Vladyslav Heraskevych believes the IOC is facing a "very big crisis."</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>How East Germany boosted Vietnam's coffee industry</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6bdc601bb903f85610984f960cfff3edbf374c121ef44d5dda1b86fee4bbe4bc</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-27T12:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-east-germany-boosted-vietnam-s-coffee-industry/a-80029974--4f080bc8669e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-east-germany-boosted-vietnam-s-coffee-industry/a-80029974?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">When East Germany could no longer afford to import coffee, it introduced a substitute blend containing rye and chicory in 1977. A public outcry ensued. The solution to the problem lay 9,000 kilometers away — in Vietnam.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>AI goes from math dunce to genius</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:427b85cb6736a6e1d82d677bb3fcdc31dffe63db859427ddd72eaf317934dc47</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-27T11:13:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ai-goes-from-math-dunce-to-genius/a-80067691--cb0cc2b981f3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ai-goes-from-math-dunce-to-genius/a-80067691?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">It once struggled to get simple sums right. But AI is now tackling tough mathematical problems like the Riemann hypothesis. How AI made this extraordinary leap — and why mathematicians should be "deeply worried."</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>German Catholic Church abuse victims may receive higher compensation</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d96f3f76b04c0214253ebea67dd84c15016cad45528e4306522203efc4e655a1</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-27T10:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/german-catholic-church-abuse-victims-may-receive-higher-compensation/a-80071917--9cefa7338ff2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/german-catholic-church-abuse-victims-may-receive-higher-compensation/a-80071917?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">In a landmark ruling, judges in Cologne found the Catholic Church responsible for abuse committed by clergy members. Victims could now be entitled to more compensation.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Albania's youth are protesting, no longer leaving the country</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:64167666bde279e5685a74f93d58351f67937fd33f24101cd8af47971cf4ca30</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-26T20:44:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/albania-s-youth-are-protesting-no-longer-leaving-the-country/a-80068939--19bf6b73472f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/albania-s-youth-are-protesting-no-longer-leaving-the-country/a-80068939?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Youth protests against a rigid political system and corruption have shaken the government of Albanian Prime Minister Edi Rama. They also show that fewer young people are willing to emigrate in search of a better future.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Trial of Berlin woman accused of spying for Russia begins after delay</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:975929c70d0f353a1ef49fba4212766d75d1c19a28e0f145a4b56aae078da704</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-26T17:44:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/trial-of-berlin-woman-accused-of-spying-for-russia-begins-after-delay/a-80057677--743246431230.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/trial-of-berlin-woman-accused-of-spying-for-russia-begins-after-delay/a-80057677?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Despite delays due to health issues, the trial of the Berlin woman accused of spying for Russia has begun. Prosecutors say the defendant used her military contacts to provide information on German defense and Ukraine.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>On farewell trip, Steinmeier calls for more investment in Africa</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:665a0cd8c089d9ad613576c6f183e720f373775b78a9f8d768e3c4e67d9934b2</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-26T17:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/on-farewell-trip-steinmeier-calls-for-more-investment-in-africa/a-80067717--a2b49bd3f417.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/on-farewell-trip-steinmeier-calls-for-more-investment-in-africa/a-80067717?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Cote d'Ivoire, Ghana, Kenya: On his last trip to Africa, outgoing German President Frank-Walter Steinmeier called on companies at home to be bolder and seize opportunities in Africa.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Freigang banned — Germany star to miss 2027 World Cup</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:060f002c21ff7ef8df384e610d89d90f5c5aa4aec791ba8d5b348b1ef1efecf3</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-26T14:50:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/freigang-banned-germany-star-to-miss-2027-world-cup/a-80063930--642807df4daf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/freigang-banned-germany-star-to-miss-2027-world-cup/a-80063930?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany forward Laura Freigang has been suspended until October 2027 after missing three doping tests, ruling her out of next year's Women's World Cup in Brazil. Freigang has denied any intention to evade controls.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>FIFA says a cyberattack against it targeted a 'limited set of personal and business information'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4eb4701d79691585778219ea34dd54556b53c877a5ffb243ac12eb22521f89cf</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-26T14:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/fifa-says-a-cyberattack-against-it-targeted-a-limited-set-of-personal-and-business-information/a-80062660--002158da7f55.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/fifa-says-a-cyberattack-against-it-targeted-a-limited-set-of-personal-and-business-information/a-80062660?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">World football's governing body says the cyberattack targeted personal and business information. They struck at a sensitive time for the under-fire organization and its president, Gianni Infantino.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>EU-Indonesia trade deal opens new markets, but challenges remain</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d43eea230ef756bbb80c26d376283d69bc89d9a044baf922e9dba42b01d4821a</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-26T13:41:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-indonesia-trade-deal-opens-new-markets-but-challenges-remain/a-80059568--6d93bfcf9a92.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-indonesia-trade-deal-opens-new-markets-but-challenges-remain/a-80059568?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The agreement offers new export and investment opportunities for Jakarta and Brussels. But can Indonesia turn Europe's growing interest in its markets and critical minerals into sustainable gains at home?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Joshua Kimmich critcizes Bayern bosses over Musiala health comments</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5395d9369ada1157426e6d30cf91463cb6e85a7edbc9e8a30cd2582f71045daa</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-26T12:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/joshua-kimmich-critcizes-bayern-bosses-over-musiala-health-comments/a-80060155--f8755c2422c2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/joshua-kimmich-critcizes-bayern-bosses-over-musiala-health-comments/a-80060155?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Joshua Kimmich has slammed Bayern Munich's leadership over comments about Jamal Musiala's health issues. The bosses have questioned whether the player can return to previous form – and is still worth his high salary.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Crew member dies after diesel tanker sinks off Ibiza coast</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:da37d17263e4382d74955c933744dbbdcea5ae9f96023aa98c7d3e87871cfe3c</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-26T11:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/crew-member-dies-after-diesel-tanker-sinks-off-ibiza-coast/a-80059054--ee7eaa5aee4e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/crew-member-dies-after-diesel-tanker-sinks-off-ibiza-coast/a-80059054?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Authorities rescued 17 crew members but one later died in hospital after a diesel tanker capsized off the Spanish island of Ibiza. A contingency plan against possible pollution damage is now in place.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Cologne court awards record damages in Catholic sex abuse case</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2f31b1fc5d51912173dd006ed359f1bb99f0be3cb4d45e1e1bad8df42725ccf2</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-26T09:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-cologne-court-awards-record-damages-in-catholic-sex-abuse-case/live-80056746--18122980124b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-cologne-court-awards-record-damages-in-catholic-sex-abuse-case/live-80056746?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A court has awarded the highest damages ever in Germany to a victim of sexual abuse linked to the Catholic Church. An alleged spy and suspected terrorists are also making headlines in Germany on Thursday.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany: 2 arrested, suspected of plotting synagogue attack</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e68559d31d2968836ab6f059c02f58af6fa1bb36765a2bbfb8c3615ebec4a8b9</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-26T09:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-2-arrested-suspected-of-plotting-synagogue-attack/a-80057715--3c7a6577a7d2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-2-arrested-suspected-of-plotting-synagogue-attack/a-80057715?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Federal prosecutors say they have ordered the arrest of two members of a pro-Iranian group on suspicion of planning an attack on a synagogue. They were detained in the cities of Heidelberg and Cologne.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Russia-Ukraine war extends to Baltic, Mediterranean</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:002091bcaaedfac26387142531c75a9df6dc8681e8f8d9737dbdccce14706ad1</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:07:32Z</updated><published>2026-11-26T09:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russia-ukraine-war-extends-to-baltic-mediterranean/a-80054604--b6459954c1cd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russia-ukraine-war-extends-to-baltic-mediterranean/a-80054604?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">By attacking Russian vessels around the world, Ukraine is trying to increase the pressure on Russia and also sending out signals to its Western allies. What is the impact on global maritime trade?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Can Rassvet, 'Russia's Starlink' change the course of the war in Ukraine?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a1d1ae1b89f31b13656e7421a7aece653f651e750717bd191fb4ec5e88518d17</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-26T05:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/can-rassvet-russia-s-starlink-change-the-course-of-the-war-in-ukraine/a-80052579--622ab8b1bc5d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/can-rassvet-russia-s-starlink-change-the-course-of-the-war-in-ukraine/a-80052579?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">SpaceX's US Starlink satellite system has played a key role in countering the Russian military in Ukraine, but now a Russian counterpart is under development. What could this mean for Ukraine?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Peter Magyar meets Volodymyr Zelenskyy: Hungary and Ukraine make a fresh start after the icy relations of the Viktor Orban era</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:79426b2afbdafd3f251ccca2a7cbb9859406a6681406efaa3fa07d55b1053e66</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-25T18:52:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/peter-magyar-meets-volodymyr-zelenskyy-hungary-and-ukraine-make-a-fresh-start-after-the-icy-relation/a-80054175--5597adb6deec.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/peter-magyar-meets-volodymyr-zelenskyy-hungary-and-ukraine-make-a-fresh-start-after-the-icy-relations-of-the-viktor-orban-era/a-80054175?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After years of frosty and hostile relations under Hungary's Kremlin-friendly former PM Viktor Orban, his successor, Peter Magyar, and Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskyy seek to reset their countries' ties.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>€561 Billion and Still Not Enough: Germany's 2027 Budget Exposes a Coalition on the Brink</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2d01d8d13d5d3b8724fee726be5128cebe5741c502592cb23398fa3115eadf4a</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-25T16:06:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/561-billion-and-still-not-enough-germany-s-2027-budget-exposes-a-coalition-on-the-brink/a-80052664--c8b0f8b87743.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/€561-billion-and-still-not-enough-germany-s-2027-budget-exposes-a-coalition-on-the-brink/a-80052664?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The budget for 2027 has reached new highs, and pension funds, defense spending and a weak economy are increasing the pressure. At the same time, tensions are mounting within the government.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>German firms eye Africa as global trade shocks hit traditional markets</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cc8cb60cdb8c9bd0d4e4617a860cff3f359167a5a663c2a933eeb8c476d5b46e</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-25T14:38:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/german-firms-eye-africa-as-global-trade-shocks-hit-traditional-markets/a-80047671--b64160bb0ab9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/german-firms-eye-africa-as-global-trade-shocks-hit-traditional-markets/a-80047671?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">German businesses are optimistic about Africa, but Berlin's cautious approach to risk is holding them back from cashing in on the opportunities that their competitors from countries like the UAE and Turkey are seizing.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Ice hockey prospect Max Calce follows Leon Draisaitl's path, leaving Mannheim for Canada</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7d0fb93436a709cb39b3996518f41c89014d2e61d7ed4efc57b4eb25e6683f09</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-25T13:28:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ice-hockey-prospect-max-calce-follows-leon-draisaitl-s-path-leaving-mannheim-for-canada/a-80049458--4ca1ab8cf6e4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ice-hockey-prospect-max-calce-follows-leon-draisaitl-s-path-leaving-mannheim-for-canada/a-80049458?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The player widely seen as Germany's biggest ice hockey talent to come along in years is leaving the country's top professional league for Canada – changing tracks in his bid to make it to the NHL.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Climate loss and damage fund exists, but the money doesn't</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1f47708ad8b33edec731d66da0dc12e43eec212061edda0d42cbd6d01f3a0dad</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-25T09:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/climate-loss-and-damage-fund-exists-but-the-money-doesn-t/a-80035620--dbacc66829c5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/climate-loss-and-damage-fund-exists-but-the-money-doesn-t/a-80035620?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Climate-vulnerable countries fought for years to create a loss and damage fund. Four years on, demand far outstrips funding, pledges are scarce, and disaster-hit nations are still waiting for support.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's women's football team take stand against domestic violence</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8cddec1549f1eccd797a1670be6e88a8384f86ecd7f9ba59731f67d4a83c4f2c</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-25T09:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-women-s-football-team-take-stand-against-domestic-violence/a-70907974--84aba926a54f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-women-s-football-team-take-stand-against-domestic-violence/a-70907974?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's women's football team are to wear UN Women badges in games against Argentina and Peru, as domestic violence hits a record high in Germany.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>German auto workers on back foot as costs, competition bite</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ca147bd776998e8922483601aa1d4115bb17aeccfe83a36dcf7ef0942d8a884e</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-25T08:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/german-auto-workers-on-back-foot-as-costs-competition-bite/a-80036111--50a0a19d14b3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/german-auto-workers-on-back-foot-as-costs-competition-bite/a-80036111?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">German auto workers profited during the industry's boom years, but are now increasingly being asked to trade past gains for future job security.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Domestic violence soars to record high in Germany</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:093960e94d3ade01a6c2e89797df4ed0eb71337ae3639048cbf2dc7802f0a5df</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-25T06:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/domestic-violence-soars-to-record-high-in-germany/a-80041678--cb6cf80357ec.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/domestic-violence-soars-to-record-high-in-germany/a-80041678?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Every three days in Germany, a man kills his wife or ex-partner. Every 10 minutes, the police record a sexual offense against a woman. "A shocking finding," according to Justice Minister Stefanie Hubig.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine's bid for NATO membership and more air defense remains controversial</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ddf73536425e910ee2c0e16f447d924c4f365fc0211b7c82c88e91119a7a7cb3</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T16:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukraine-s-bid-for-nato-membership-and-more-air-defense-remains-controversial/a-80029852--1abf02560b4b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-s-bid-for-nato-membership-and-more-air-defense-remains-controversial/a-80029852?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskyy is calling for the rapid acceptance of his country into NATO. However, the necessary unanimity for this is lacking, as shown during the NATO Parliamentary Assembly in Berlin.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>EU enlargement: Why do some EU member states use their vetoes to block the accession of certain candidate countries?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:92803055dd208b9b8d88aac25bb4b40f7d9d0c4e5cb36efbe1dab64bdff4ed8b</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T14:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-enlargement-why-do-some-eu-member-states-use-their-vetoes-to-block-the-accession-of-certain-candi/a-80034401--27cd622204d3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-enlargement-why-do-some-eu-member-states-use-their-vetoes-to-block-the-accession-of-certain-candidate-countries/a-80034401?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Individual EU member states use their veto powers to block candidate countries in the accession process — often for reasons of domestic politics. DW takes a look at some cases and examines what's behind them.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>CAS reinstates Senegal as 2025 AFCON champions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fc29d47c7e8d189897203880e4a9a4f78ce7af5964a55a3f09d4b4f5aad596c0</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T14:42:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/cas-reinstates-senegal-as-2025-afcon-champions/a-80021027--561a21777065.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/cas-reinstates-senegal-as-2025-afcon-champions/a-80021027?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Court of Arbitration for Sport has reinstated Senegal as 2025 AFCON champions, overturning a CAF decision that stripped them of the title. Morocco, previously declared winners, are confirmed runners-up.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Bombed factories, billion-dollar opportunity: Why German companies are staying in Ukraine</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:50624c7100b2ccec37f261455d5e289606f6946c6494a8e22dc93803e2f71202</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T11:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bombed-factories-billion-dollar-opportunity-why-german-companies-are-staying-in-ukraine/a-80030201--13f674deb921.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bombed-factories-billion-dollar-opportunity-why-german-companies-are-staying-in-ukraine/a-80030201?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">German companies remain committed to Ukraine despite million-dollar losses, an unreliable energy supply and a shortage of skilled workers. They are betting on new markets and long-term growth.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>How cautious investors are struggling to avoid the AI bubble</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4c02879edf2de21f28acf4c23db9aa8b344110a0ca76963df3a1f55350d05655</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T10:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-cautious-investors-are-struggling-to-avoid-the-ai-bubble/a-80016412--863307befc9b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-cautious-investors-are-struggling-to-avoid-the-ai-bubble/a-80016412?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">From Nvidia to Coreweave, AI and tech stocks have swung sharply in recent months. Some investors still see plenty of room to run, while others are trying to diversify — and finding it harder than expected.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>German directors' doc on stolen film wins International Emmy Award</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:789ad99fe845f8d51f4456a456f02133ec35b8a3326c44d239efd34afc8b63ad</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T09:41:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/german-directors-doc-on-stolen-film-wins-international-emmy-award/a-76103455--80792ca0c998.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/german-directors-doc-on-stolen-film-wins-international-emmy-award/a-76103455?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Two German film students confronted the American who won festival prizes with their animated movie. "The Talented Mr. F," their documentary on their fight against plagiarism, is now in the spotlight.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>What happens if a nuclear weapon explodes in space?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0dfb4406cfa5b103e1eae233f494fb75d11d2e0ea3017e6ffd90acdc8c7a25d4</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T08:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/what-happens-if-a-nuclear-weapon-explodes-in-space/a-80025827--a6201a0063e7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/what-happens-if-a-nuclear-weapon-explodes-in-space/a-80025827?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Earth's atmosphere offers protection from a nuclear blast in space, but satellites are more exposed. We explain how radiation could damage them, why the effects can linger and what protection is possible.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>Weapons, war and wavering trust: Germans want to see more restraint in foreign policy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c080fe989051126614d0ac4e040d48ce9020a663ec37cd95005df5d8b824c4fa</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T05:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/weapons-war-and-wavering-trust-germans-want-to-see-more-restraint-in-foreign-policy/a-80026254--66b3f174435c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/weapons-war-and-wavering-trust-germans-want-to-see-more-restraint-in-foreign-policy/a-80026254?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">According to a study by the Körber Foundation, a growing number of Germans now oppose providing military aid to Ukraine. The majority also believes that Germany should take a neutral position between the US and China.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>US and UK to host Women's World Cups in 2031 and 2035</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d213e4c246ff3eaebeef3fb8b9a5a67bbe46f7e526b0dc06194e028c5bccdee2</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T16:19:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-and-uk-to-host-women-s-world-cups-in-2031-and-2035/a-80023786--81630f151694.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-and-uk-to-host-women-s-world-cups-in-2031-and-2035/a-80023786?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">FIFA has confirmed the United States, Mexico, Costa Rica and Jamaica will host the 2031 Women's World Cup — the first to feature 48 teams. The UK will stage the 2035 edition, its first World Cup since 1966.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Gukesh to defend chess crown against rising star Sindarov</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e6736fca4ec4abe45aa56d3b5ba42a78bbd76c423a7157516c8d1f10f3135644</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T15:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/gukesh-to-defend-chess-crown-against-rising-star-sindarov/a-80021806--07e5204aa07f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/gukesh-to-defend-chess-crown-against-rising-star-sindarov/a-80021806?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As the World Chess championship gets underway, it's no coincidence that the titleholder, Gukesh Dommaraju, and his challenger, Jakhovir Sindarov, are both from Asia.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Nvidia reinstates former CEO Jensen Huang despite China espionage scandal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9e2eb7d21502ba380a77c0cb357a42168a30771671c0567191767f73cc3650c1</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z<