uganda-minister-at-cop31-we-need-a-just-transition/a-79997209?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Funding from wealthy countries to help deal with the impacts of climate change hasn't materialized, says Uganda's environment minister. The East African country is hoping oil and carbon credits will help boost finances.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>COP deadlock prompts calls for a reset of climate diplomacy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6b4fde327c0bffb8435dd36fb877d45956aae6f87c6f5d5d2d31549a32bef3c7</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T13:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/cop-deadlock-prompts-calls-for-a-reset-of-climate-diplomacy/a-80020494--3b4f8cad49dc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/cop-deadlock-prompts-calls-for-a-reset-of-climate-diplomacy/a-80020494?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">COP31 has been branded a failure after countries couldn't reach a final agreement, divided over a reference to "fossil fuels." But was the decision to walk away from a watered-down text actually a show of strength?</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>German police respond to multiple school bomb threats</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d380ef0c69ce36676f88fd970e497572996e790d91e94a146c4c7eac9146145c</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T11:01:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/german-police-respond-to-multiple-school-bomb-threats/a-80018842--56ba1301d92a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/german-police-respond-to-multiple-school-bomb-threats/a-80018842?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Police in Germany are responding to bomb threats against a series of schools, but say that at present they don't believe them to be credible. Danish authorities are reporting a similar series of apparent hoaxes.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>'I've lost her forever' — Why German voice actors are refusing to sign Netflix's AI contract</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:12f54b4095e11988137f4f2b230ab73218c62f1666a299534759844088e34d3d</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T10:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/i-ve-lost-her-forever-why-german-voice-actors-are-refusing-to-sign-netflix-s-ai-contract/a-80004381--da3277b6e37b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/i-ve-lost-her-forever-why-german-voice-actors-are-refusing-to-sign-netflix-s-ai-contract/a-80004381?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">For decades, Germans have known Hollywood's biggest stars through the same familiar voices. Now an AI clause in Netflix contracts is splitting the industry over whether it protects performers or exposes them.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Budget cuts threaten Germany's fight against antisemitism and racism</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8e1f0cd37982731e13e73abaadf4c8d755083834b7e4a8515f7cd3d2471caa1e</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T10:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/budget-cuts-threaten-germany-s-fight-against-antisemitism-and-racism/a-80018644--fcf379d5b1d2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/budget-cuts-threaten-germany-s-fight-against-antisemitism-and-racism/a-80018644?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Numerous grassroots initiatives in Germany are facing funding cuts. Affected organizations are sounding the alarm, pointing to growing challenges posed by far-right extremism.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Rembrandt's 'The Night Watch' is more alive than you'd expect</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2396e1cba8801948b568adcb9f6ccb8d6b5c28f6b6c6cc233fed10e8d0a05b7a</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T10:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/rembrandt-s-the-night-watch-is-more-alive-than-you-d-expect/a-79972540--0d1ff511f0b9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/rembrandt-s-the-night-watch-is-more-alive-than-you-d-expect/a-79972540?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A new project and exhibition, "The Night Watch Lives," lifts the veil on the hidden world of microbes covering one of the most famous paintings of the Dutch Golden Age.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's Early Start Pension: Can child investment accounts help?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c869fc12c6eda89363fc624c13d3163f39bc2d7cc0730791f3d7204f9d8a1577</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T09:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-early-start-pension-can-child-investment-accounts-help/a-79852185--25ffc2424261.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-early-start-pension-can-child-investment-accounts-help/a-79852185?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany plans to pay €10 a month into investment accounts for children to encourage long-term retirement saving. Economists say the measure may help build wealth but won't solve the country's pension funding challenge.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Metalworkers go on strike as pay dispute heats up</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bed514248cb5150da7f4a05577f283bf859fb8ede53ee7af88f153cc2e7939e8</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T07:11:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-metalworkers-go-on-strike-as-pay-dispute-heats-up/live-80015633--a1790c046188.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-metalworkers-go-on-strike-as-pay-dispute-heats-up/live-80015633?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's biggest union is calling for more strikes over heated pay disputes with car makers like Mercedes and shipyards among the companies impacted. Meanwhile, a Berlin hospital fire leaves many injured.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Rule-breaking is contagious — and good examples barely help</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:158084693ec0388d790e43a1e0438f0ba06ea6fc8f86dcc3599ed2a4cfeedc5a</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T06:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/rule-breaking-is-contagious-and-good-examples-barely-help/a-79980025--098488c374ac.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/rule-breaking-is-contagious-and-good-examples-barely-help/a-79980025?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Seeing someone break a rule makes people more likely to break it too, a new study has found, especially when the rule-breaker is on their side politically. Watching others behave well barely made a difference.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>COP31 climate talks end without consensus on how to fund vulnerable countries or move the world away from coal, oil and gas use</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2b41dc6d71600421f62e5dee5bd35aa2a73dc2171c59de8707a8735f8282f491</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-22T13:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/cop31-climate-talks-end-without-consensus-on-how-to-fund-vulnerable-countries-or-move-the-world-away/a-80003610--d912dc284aaa.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/cop31-climate-talks-end-without-consensus-on-how-to-fund-vulnerable-countries-or-move-the-world-away-from-coal-oil-and-gas-use/a-80003610?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After two weeks of tough talks, the COP31 climate summit has closed without a consensus on how to quit fossil fuels or fund countries struggling to adapt to a hotter world.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Inspired by Bernie Sanders: A German agency is using US-Style campaigning to boost the left in 2029</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9896ff646f6aee10f98d1ffa60578e00bf9fafb1c606e2b41df1f6f5a4511f64</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-22T08:39:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/inspired-by-bernie-sanders-a-german-agency-is-using-us-style-campaigning-to-boost-the-left-in-2029/a-80001443--f6cd4061ee72.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/inspired-by-bernie-sanders-a-german-agency-is-using-us-style-campaigning-to-boost-the-left-in-2029/a-80001443?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">"The Goodforces" wants to see a swing to the left in the 2029 German elections. The agency counts New York Mayor Zohran Mamdani and Bernie Sanders among its inspirations. Could it transform the political landscape?</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: IG Metall union calls for new 24-hour strike</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:06468981b17a05acd9fdaa3552a926ddf2479846645f620e697d507780b4fc1a</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-22T08:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-ig-metall-union-calls-for-new-24-hour-strike/live-80008430--32c896775229.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-ig-metall-union-calls-for-new-24-hour-strike/live-80008430?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's biggest single union, IG Metall, is calling on car and shipyard workers to strike amid a pay row. Meanwhile, Germany's president is setting off on an Africa trip. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><en