maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">European Council President Antonio Costa has proposed a smaller EU budget for 2028-2034, including a 3% tax on major digital firms to ease member states' contributions. France has already rejected the plan as inadequate.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Russia strikes Zelenskyy's hometown, killing 2</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:05a9d81b5026170729d1f9a2a3c769bc588e8d21ac2824252c12ed98b156b6b7</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-21T14:44:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russia-strikes-zelenskyy-s-hometown-killing-2/a-80009458--1c5b88d83c35.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russia-strikes-zelenskyy-s-hometown-killing-2/a-80009458?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The attacks follow Russian President Vladimir Putin's vow of a "painful" response to Ukraine's attacks this week on the Kerch Bridge, linking Russian-occupied Crimea.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's religious freedom report: Authoritarian regimes, holy wars, and spies abroad</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9a16d6db2357542dd5e4ebf6f4558b86afd8d5dd19722fc4611d6655476309c3</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-21T12:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-religious-freedom-report-authoritarian-regimes-holy-wars-and-spies-abroad/a-79995216--a4dc5259a9cd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-religious-freedom-report-authoritarian-regimes-holy-wars-and-spies-abroad/a-79995216?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Harassment, persecution, surveillance: Across much of the world, people of faith are facing growing pressure. A new German government report is unusually direct in criticizing China in particular.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Russian ornithologist jailed over small donations to Navalny's foundation</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4c9b805c65a2ea023ac724b457aaec8d46ceec07474c24ca17148873cb18aadc</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T20:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russian-ornithologist-jailed-over-small-donations-to-navalny-s-foundation/a-80005505--49dba4e1f94e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russian-ornithologist-jailed-over-small-donations-to-navalny-s-foundation/a-80005505?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Sofia Rosenfeld has devoted her life to studying Arctic birds. A Russian court sentenced her to 3.5 years in a penal colony over donations to Navalny's foundation. Friends and family are fighting for her release.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>COP31: No agreement on climate science, disinformation spreading</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d64de87007fe55bd7900ddc85436878b69fa1a3ddfe2dd435c8b287233a16c83</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T20:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/cop31-no-agreement-on-climate-science-disinformation-spreading/a-80004894--cd9d23743160.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/cop31-no-agreement-on-climate-science-disinformation-spreading/a-80004894?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Attacks on climate science and disinformation risk delaying key measures at COP31 in Antalya. As the UN climate talks draw to a close, how will that affect efforts to come to an agreement?</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Has the 'Parthenon puzzle' been solved? The long quest to reassemble lost eastern pediment</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:da13b720fb87686aee7efa75ba6cf2badca341c71b827c959e47adfe6c6e580a</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T20:03:00Z</published>