 have agreed on "landmark" deals on youth mobility and trade. Leaders on both sides praised the agreement as they seek to rebuild ties.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Turkey takes control of opposition broadcaster Sozcu TV</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9d93ecc62f74b715941a82db031608367fa85a9487c239294cd0c8a900eceb8e</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T14:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/turkey-takes-control-of-opposition-broadcaster-sozcu-tv/a-80001984--d9f6e0119d22.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/turkey-takes-control-of-opposition-broadcaster-sozcu-tv/a-80001984?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">In the latest in a series of raids and arrests, another major pro-opposition Turkish broadcaster has been brought under state control. This is the third in a year.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>FIFA presidential election 2027: Infantino facing Diallo and Tashima — could an alliance change everything?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e993c89aaf71d442578c2cf50f0890e711373e7a05fd994ddfe393f2a57fa7c7</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T12:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/fifa-presidential-election-2027-infantino-facing-diallo-and-tashima-could-an-alliance-change-everyth/a-80002882--01040a665cff.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/fifa-presidential-election-2027-infantino-facing-diallo-and-tashima-could-an-alliance-change-everything/a-80002882?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Two challengers to Gianni Infantino have registered for next year's FIFA presidential election. What do Philippe Diallo and Kozo Tashima stand for – and do they stand a chance against the incumbent?</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Lufthansa to cut 1,000 jobs, citing ongoing losses — reports</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:73a9b2b11567ab496b3daead5ae5406326110b4f3a15a07e11e70d333ee8623b</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T09:43:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/lufthansa-to-cut-1-000-jobs-citing-ongoing-losses-reports/a-80000062--a7b4260396ca.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/lufthansa-to-cut-1-000-jobs-citing-ongoing-losses-reports/a-80000062?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">According to a letter obtained by the media, Lufthansa's executive board said the German company is losing €20 million every month. In addition to job cuts, operational cuts are also planned.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Have we missed our chance to stop climate change?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f03d9c03c2c9cd96843e7029817c55ca96888fe4fc96930b6b0fc075976e428b</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T09:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/have-we-missed-our-chance-to-stop-climate-change/a-79986199--68173e73a2c9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/have-we-missed-our-chance-to-stop-climate-change/a-79986199?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">From record-breaking heat to devastating floods and wildfires, the warning signs are everywhere. Can rising temperatures still be brought under control?</summary><category term="Climate" /></entry><entry><title>Putin proposes second humanitarian ceasefire — is it a trap?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a1f52c1a7cab42e331837de2d460c084712cc838d7bacd57a5b8a52975b30873</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T20:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/putin-proposes-second-humanitarian-ceasefire-is-it-a-trap/a-79996772--e715071e3f54.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/putin-proposes-second-humanitarian-ceasefire-is-it-a-trap/a-79996772?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Russian President Putin has suggested evacuating civilians from the embattled Ukrainian city of Kostiantynivka. But experts warn this could serve military, not humanitarian, aims. What should Kyiv do?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>No mention of fossil fuels in latest COP31 draft deal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2374ac1151e7f23e51e70aa6462702c179c17b7c35c31a686bb901b1fd2fbc76</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T16:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/no-mention-of-fossil-fuels-in-latest-cop31-draft-deal/a-79992394--36cfb19df8f5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/no-mention-of-fossil-fuels-in-latest-cop31-draft-deal/a-79992394?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">One of the most fraught debates at the UN climate talks in Turkey has revolved around the future of coal, oil and gas. Now, all mention of fossil fuels has been removed from the summit's new draft agreement.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Anthropic trading tests investors' appetite for AI</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2a02b931fb70f439bd460fad9bdbff91f26bdfc6b813991938690422a7d4a37d</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T15:52:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/anthropic-trading-tests-investors-appetite-for-ai/a-79993163--d18c2700770b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/anthropic-trading-tests-investors-appetite-for-ai/a-79993163?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Anthropic was valued at $2 trillion after shares started trading on the Nasdaq following a record $81 billion IPO. Its performance will put investor confidence in AI to the test.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Alexander Zverev faces fresh lawsuit from ex-girlfriend</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ec5290bebefe258bbc8c16c2caf4666bb5b4a400753e5bf2cac281c95a14ec63</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T15:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/alexander-zverev-faces-fresh-lawsuit-from-ex-girlfriend/a-79990005--d63dbeaa4aae.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/alexander-zverev-faces-fresh-lawsuit-from-ex-girlfriend/a-79990005?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">World No. 1 tennis player Alexander Zverev is facing a new lawsuit related to a domestic abuse trial. The lawyer for his ex-girlfriend, Brenda Patea, told DW what the allegations are against the German player.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>EU Commission confirms it was targeted in cyberattack using AI tools</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6f93ec71336ad88dce92239ab2a06b4dd58c93096e2b13f648eafe4d89f05a20</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T14:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-commission-confirms-it-was-targeted-in-cyberattack-using-ai-tools/a-79993016--2e1cd85b257c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-commission-confirms-it-was-targeted-in-cyberattack-using-ai-tools/a-79993016?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The European Commission was targeted by an "AI-generated cybercampaign," a spokesperson has said. This is the first time the bloc has publicly reported an AI-based cyberattack.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Wadephul: 'Coalition of the Willing' talks in Berlin send strong signal to Moscow</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:aa1d92da5d9f4823d3487821a9b9da14b3fca1bf20335616ceab4e5769bd4deb</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T13:56:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/wadephul-coalition-of-the-willing-talks-in-berlin-send-strong-signal-to-moscow/a-79990664--ce1ce93ebd6c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/wadephul-coalition-of-the-willing-talks-in-berlin-send-strong-signal-to-moscow/a-79990664?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">German Foreign Minister Wadephul has said the Coalition of the Willing meeting in Berlin sends a clear message to Moscow to take peace talks seriously. He also warned Ukraine should be prepared for peace talks to fail.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Iran balances ties with China and Russia as Trump ramps up pressure</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a83322918f75f468167b04c591dc33d90c939b7ee18ca0ac7d5bca983f62be7b</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T09:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-balances-ties-with-china-and-russia-as-trump-ramps-up-pressure/a-79979920--3c92417b16df.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-balances-ties-with-china-and-russia-as-trump-ramps-up-pressure/a-79979920?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As Donald Trump seeks to tighten economic pressure on Iran, China remains its biggest oil customer and Russia a key partner. But both powers are balancing support for Tehran against broader interests with Washington.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Is the AI bubble bursting just as Anthropic goes public?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:48a412ed91a48a629e68db30c22960227c24f4a67516e381fd917d2fb4bb14ac</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T05:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/is-the-ai-bubble-bursting-just-as-anthropic-goes-public/a-79896537--10f78cdc2264.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/is-the-ai-bubble-bursting-just-as-anthropic-goes-public/a-79896537?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The sharp sell-off in tech stocks after the US midterms and the Nvidia scandal has cast doubt on Anthropic's IPO. Yet with hundreds of billions still being invested, some think the AI party is still in full swing.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Borussia Dortmund bows to fan pressure and end Rheinmetall deal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b4f39f07a510f56a9a47a288417de94d7d41dcb2bc842219d33a47fbd9313a59</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T15:39:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/borussia-dortmund-bows-to-fan-pressure-and-end-rheinmetall-deal/a-79980121--2c9b64a964f9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/borussia-dortmund-bows-to-fan-pressure-and-end-rheinmetall-deal/a-79980121?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Borussia Dortmund has reluctantly ended its association with a major sponsor after long-term fan protests. They are not the first Bundesliga club to u-turn, as commercial interests clash with politics and fan culture.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>'Coalition of the Willing' meets in Berlin: Europe remains committed to Ukraine</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f3930016df5419612ec1f079beac48cf1683a3134ce50e18048aff1ca80e1e56</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T15:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/coalition-of-the-willing-meets-in-berlin-europe-remains-committed-to-ukraine/a-79974996--9529e6865e8b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/coalition-of-the-willing-meets-in-berlin-europe-remains-committed-to-ukraine/a-79974996?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The "Coalition of the Willing" supporting Ukraine is gathering in Berlin. One of the key issues under discussion is whether Europe will be able to play a role in future negotiations over the country's future.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>How a green economy could help reverse climate change</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e043ed9c0ddbf4d1fdd68bfaab62ed4d2084d70113bce2043bf3494845224e95</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T09:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-a-green-economy-could-help-reverse-climate-change/a-79874576--23cc55e56fdb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-a-green-economy-could-help-reverse-climate-change/a-79874576?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Green growth promises a future in which economies thrive without destroying the environment. But is this vision realistic?</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Hashim Thaci's second conviction in The Hague reignites debate in Kosovo about justice and the Kosovo Specialist Chambers</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:62ca4d58f95e9441afda71ec173e5e553225f117848b93ec1226608750573f7c</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-17T20:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/hashim-thaci-s-second-conviction-in-the-hague-reignites-debate-in-kosovo-about-justice-and-the-kosov/a-79975227--3db3936546e0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/hashim-thaci-s-second-conviction-in-the-hague-reignites-debate-in-kosovo-about-justice-and-the-kosovo-specialist-chambers/a-79975227?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Former President Hashim Thaci has been convicted of trying to influence witnesses in his war crimes trial. The conviction has reignited debate in Kosovo about the Kosovo Specialist Chambers, the court that convicted him.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Nvidia forms national security committee after Huang affair</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bed6e5c5be595ca55a66449c812d9a5d330505fc29e7b715c00a93a01c3fb985</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-17T14:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nvidia-forms-national-security-committee-after-huang-affair/a-79970447--7d1c93df3ff0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nvidia-forms-national-security-committee-after-huang-affair/a-79970447?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Nvidia has created a board-level committee for national security and export control. This follows the resignation of CEO Jensen Huang over extramarital affairs, allegedly including one with a Chinese intelligence asset.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Klopp and Wirtz offer glimpse of bright German future</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b358b03ee94e66b9ffffb0ef526dccbc70109ffc5af570840ee423e3f04e67fb</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-17T11:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/klopp-and-wirtz-offer-glimpse-of-bright-german-future/a-79968184--a5059b3200c7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/klopp-and-wirtz-offer-glimpse-of-bright-german-future/a-79968184?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's fall from grace in recent years has seen the team drift away from the fans. But Monday's drubbing of the Netherlands and the impact of Jürgen Klopp, Florian Wirtz and emerging youngsters offers hope.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Could the Airbus €3 billion loan row reignite a US-EU trade dispute?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bf18014d48c649cabd8bdfd1cf4ab511d5438163078047d42026f6015b0fce62</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-17T11:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/could-the-airbus-_3-billion-loan-row-reignite-a-us-eu-trade-dispute/a-79943075--30f362f3b820.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/could-the-airbus-€3-billion-loan-row-reignite-a-us-eu-trade-dispute/a-79943075?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The US says a record €3 billion financing package for Airbus may conflict with a transatlantic aircraft-subsidy truce. EU officials insist the funding complies with market-based rules.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Plans for Rwanda migrant hub come under fire</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8f4df4413d99d271b45423510caf13fb970116276caf68fcf459776edc972fd2</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-17T10:15:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-plans-for-rwanda-migrant-hub-come-under-fire/live-79965639--9c6685ac3d74.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-plans-for-rwanda-migrant-hub-come-under-fire/live-79965639?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Human rights groups have slammed plans by Germany and four other EU states to send rejected asylum seekers to Rwanda. In other news, business start-ups in Germany are on track to reach the highest level since 2015.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>France's Philippe Diallo to challenge Infantino for FIFA presidency</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2871b69e7852dd24ef6eebf7cd00448e939ba49c3ef1af11be0f83f7fa1e529d</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T20:24:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/france-s-philippe-diallo-to-challenge-infantino-for-fifa-presidency/a-79962843--6fe08ae5c0bf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/france-s-philippe-diallo-to-challenge-infantino-for-fifa-presidency/a-79962843?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Philippe Diallo is the second candidate to stand against incumbent Gianni Infantino. He is backed by European football's governing body UEFA, known to be critical of Infantino.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>NASA's Voyager 1 reaches a light-day away from Earth</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6a9fd2146fcf45ed39a88d60891792fc7cd5bc7668bab2be2dda3b9564b624bc</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T17:24:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nasa-s-voyager-1-reaches-a-light-day-away-from-earth/a-79961817--190e9087abf2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nasa-s-voyager-1-reaches-a-light-day-away-from-earth/a-79961817?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">When just saying 'hello' takes a two-day round trip, you're a light-day, or 26 billion kilometers, from Earth. Only one human-made object has ever traveled that far — and its journey into interstellar space continues.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>What has changed in James Bond films over the decades</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:49ad6c3636efa68b599901590663bdb97480647ea647f8fe4bb1bfbc4d0890f1</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T17:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/what-has-changed-in-james-bond-films-over-the-decades/a-63332001--7d894a9cd4fe.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/what-has-changed-in-james-bond-films-over-the-decades/a-63332001?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">In 1962, a martini-drinking womanizer saved the world for the first time in "Dr. No." As Robert Pattinson takes on the role of 007, here's how the films evolved.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>COP31 draft deal calls for 'immediate' shift away from fossil fuels</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:77c30bb9416e175255f3f09e706b2dd5c0b3780abaf9e6a3643fe05052f562d8</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T14:05:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/cop31-draft-deal-calls-for-immediate-shift-away-from-fossil-fuels/a-79960705--2a7f1bfc2c85.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/cop31-draft-deal-calls-for-immediate-shift-away-from-fossil-fuels/a-79960705?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The preliminary agreement at UN climate talks in Turkey calls for a rapid reduction of planet-warming emissions and at least $120 billion to help countries adapt to climate change.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Klopp wants Infantino out as FIFA candidate deadline looms</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4ebf65beef74c46a0e2cba7b30bf1b9f7e12431c7fcfa4627083004bf5f3aa46</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T11:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/klopp-wants-infantino-out-as-fifa-candidate-deadline-looms/a-79958229--458d3356c9f8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/klopp-wants-infantino-out-as-fifa-candidate-deadline-looms/a-79958229?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany coach Jürgen Klopp has joined the chorus of football figures critical of FIFA President Gianni Infantino. But with time running out, there are few who seem willing to run against him.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Can a 'coalition of the willing' create momentum for a fossil fuel phaseout?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:451290b2e30d1d2f61fd0a6294b336c263936ff64ed640e390dbcbfe66d0c25d</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T08:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/can-a-coalition-of-the-willing-create-momentum-for-a-fossil-fuel-phaseout/a-79926748--1f05ab68dfcb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/can-a-coalition-of-the-willing-create-momentum-for-a-fossil-fuel-phaseout/a-79926748?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">In April, about 60 countries held an unprecedented meeting in Colombia to work out a plan to slowly quit oil, coal and gas. How influential is this coalition at the COP31 climate summit?</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Wolf Biermann at 90: The singer who defied East Germany</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f27f675382402a7f7ee5e23b0f8b2ea6c89a6957331957c005ca276f07142f05</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T10:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/wolf-biermann-at-90-the-singer-who-defied-east-germany/a-79915297--17726feda083.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/wolf-biermann-at-90-the-singer-who-defied-east-germany/a-79915297?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">His life is a reflection of contemporary German history, addressed via his songs and sharp wit. At 90, he's as feisty as ever.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>What's going on with the polar vortex?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5df8e9492c33e874e41b811cc466bcfc41be99e0c2b6cd86d661f217e879bafd</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T16:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/what-s-going-on-with-the-polar-vortex/a-79943105--6a28f0640609.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/what-s-going-on-with-the-polar-vortex/a-79943105?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Observations show the ring of fierce winds that rotate at the Earth's North Pole has changed direction. Scientists say it's a historic disruption and the earliest reversal on record. What could it mean for the weather?</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Ice hockey impasse as Russia threatens sanctions on Canada, Germany</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ebce1a353b4ce9e5a072a7fac34f977dcd8554a47f19f344bd9cd8bf03205354</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T16:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ice-hockey-impasse-as-russia-threatens-sanctions-on-canada-germany/a-79942676--52aad908ad79.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ice-hockey-impasse-as-russia-threatens-sanctions-on-canada-germany/a-79942676?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Two weeks after the CAS ordered ice hockey's governing body to reintegrate Russia into international play, a solution remains elusive. Now Russia has threatened to take legal action against two tournament hosts.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's Nmecha won't repeat controversial goal celebration</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5f0b199cafda31aac409bfae55ac63e9fa7ff855596e4a3f57b47026cba0efba</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T11:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-nmecha-won-t-repeat-controversial-goal-celebration/a-79937994--cc5ab533247b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-nmecha-won-t-repeat-controversial-goal-celebration/a-79937994?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany head coach Jürgen Klopp has said midfielder Felix Nmecha will not repeat a goal celebration that sparked controversy over the past week. Germany are set to face Serbia and the Netherlands in the Nations League.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Could lack of money sink TFFF rainforest fund before it even launches?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2ce451411ab893eab8d6be053b5cd9f033a127f6f03c11977a4db7234bce757c</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T08:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/could-lack-of-money-sink-tfff-rainforest-fund-before-it-even-launches/a-79878673--227abf2cebee.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/could-lack-of-money-sink-tfff-rainforest-fund-before-it-even-launches/a-79878673?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The TFFF rainforest fund aims to make forest conservation more profitable than deforestation. But a lack of money may prevent it from getting off the ground.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Iranian activist and Nobel Peace Prize winner Narges Mohammadi shares her story in memoir</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4ab8e2b40260dffb9f5d4cc58090d68f6a67f6c8a3b16485dd16d0696a1ffb0b</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T08:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iranian-activist-and-nobel-peace-prize-winner-narges-mohammadi-shares-her-story-in-memoir/a-79868167--a983bd7e2dcc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iranian-activist-and-nobel-peace-prize-winner-narges-mohammadi-shares-her-story-in-memoir/a-79868167?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Written and smuggled out of prison, the 2023 Nobel Prize laureate's memoir reveals the cost of defying Iran's regime and fighting for freedom.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Jensen Huang: Spy row, affairs leave Nvidia without its rockstar CEO</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:abd087e8d5d781a68353847bc88b4e3cdbf97e3a57c1e990376fd88a51efcae8</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T15:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/jensen-huang-spy-row-affairs-leave-nvidia-without-its-rockstar-ceo/a-79926972--e6a7da621d57.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/jensen-huang-spy-row-affairs-leave-nvidia-without-its-rockstar-ceo/a-79926972?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Jensen Huang, who built Nvidia into the world’s dominant AI chipmaker, is stepping down as CEO over extramarital affairs. DW examines how losing its figurehead will affect the firm and the US-China AI race.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>What are fossil fuels?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8feede44b63e3836545601dce94f72b204969414a9023570f3170c87f04e9939</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T12:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/what-are-fossil-fuels/a-67970540--1920eabf4714.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/what-are-fossil-fuels/a-67970540?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">They are in our shampoo bottles, power our cars and heat our homes. But what actually are fossil fuels, and why do they matter?</summary><category term="Climate" /></entry><entry><title>Intelligent women get less help at work, study finds</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0247ab6596a4299f7a2290f89f1588dd5507abd31df17d27d28ae87ad7e8d326</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T07:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/intelligent-women-get-less-help-at-work-study-finds/a-79910881--d3f9551f1647.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/intelligent-women-get-less-help-at-work-study-finds/a-79910881?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Women who scored high on intelligence tests were seen as more hostile by their teammates and got less help, a new study finds. High-scoring men faced no such penalty. Research explains why.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>Is AIIB's complaint mechanism failing affected communities?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:29ede6cd734494378a8f4c971c9f497ea709237fa3b817bd1992d64a4a31a4e0</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T15:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/is-aiib-s-complaint-mechanism-failing-affected-communities/a-79919917--1bfa788b7764.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/is-aiib-s-complaint-mechanism-failing-affected-communities/a-79919917?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Asian Infrastructure Investment Bank has a grievance redress mechanism for people affected by projects it finances. But those seeking to file a complaint face significant hurdles. Critics say reforms are needed.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Can global leaders put their money where their mouth is on climate?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:79ae5e70dd20111ec92d71a91dc1a461f976ef52cbcaf1fc5102cc232c29df1f</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T14:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/can-global-leaders-put-their-money-where-their-mouth-is-on-climate/a-79918744--b2fe82b3dbb0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/can-global-leaders-put-their-money-where-their-mouth-is-on-climate/a-79918744?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">World leaders warn that geopolitical divisions are distracting from the climate crisis as negotiations focus on clean energy and financing, while Iran calls for compensation for war-related environmental damage.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>DW Science explainer on the default mode network: what your brain does when you aren't focusing on anything, and why it's important.</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1cd8bc2d8fdb89df65f8cf6bdf90cadfda7c218a7b38436fb33bb4d9c5c60c6e</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T06:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/dw-science-explainer-on-the-default-mode-network-what-your-brain-does-when-you-aren-t-focusing-on-an/a-79908787--cf91bcf53b1d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/dw-science-explainer-on-the-default-mode-network-what-your-brain-does-when-you-aren-t-focusing-on-anything-and-why-it-s-important/a-79908787?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Doing nothing might be the ultimate brain hack. When you're bored, the brain goes into default mode network. It's not only healthy for you, but it may also shape the very essence of your identity.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>Germany slips in climate protection rankings as other countries make gains</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3aba3bb788085b93e71965ea0533d98eba0ac5e42140035a4904bfd9aaca3d2a</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T06:41:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-slips-in-climate-protection-rankings-as-other-countries-make-gains/a-79913635--edb7d622928e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-slips-in-climate-protection-rankings-as-other-countries-make-gains/a-79913635?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Record renewable energy growth is driving climate progress in some countries, but Germany and many major emitters are falling behind.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Controversial kinship: From colonial rule to the Holocaust?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5928c786253c35dfacbdafb9ba0fd02bf1288b2b586408f4b16d8b831eb8bc61</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T15:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/controversial-kinship-from-colonial-rule-to-the-holocaust/a-79902228--16129c6452e2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/controversial-kinship-from-colonial-rule-to-the-holocaust/a-79902228?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Hitler once called Eastern Europe "Germany's India." A new exhibition examines the links between colonialism and Nazism, and the bitter debate over where comparisons illuminate history and where they fall short.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Neuer injury gives Urbig chance to shape Bayern and Germany future</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:edc2d50430b91ea26bde9293bfd6273866f84b54fae3a1276eaee49c3c756a56</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T15:13:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/neuer-injury-gives-urbig-chance-to-shape-bayern-and-germany-future/a-79910042--b0a77bac4246.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/neuer-injury-gives-urbig-chance-to-shape-bayern-and-germany-future/a-79910042?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Manuel Neuer's latest injury gives Jonas Urbig a run of games in Bayern's goal. Marc-André ter Stegen remains Germany’s No. 1, but Urbig now has a chance to strengthen his case for the future.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Megaspeed and the battle to go high-end Nvidia chips into China</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8653c746808904868fed3882a9f8a5c2a78398ac19451a9650f120656140eb5f</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T14:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/megaspeed-and-the-battle-to-go-high-end-nvidia-chips-into-china/a-79909129--5e400fbb45fc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/megaspeed-and-the-battle-to-go-high-end-nvidia-chips-into-china/a-79909129?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Jensen Huang's affair with a suspected Chinese spy has shone a light on Megaspeed, the company she worked for. It is under investigation in the US for smuggling Nvidia chips into China, which it denies.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Borussia Dortmund's Felix Nmecha and the question of religion</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f36120b23d51b59c691959a355ce2fb95d9d7fcaab26725215f7da06aeffad83</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T11:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/borussia-dortmund-s-felix-nmecha-and-the-question-of-religion/a-79900432--cd7bb6e11389.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/borussia-dortmund-s-felix-nmecha-and-the-question-of-religion/a-79900432?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Felix Nmecha's "Crowns down" celebration has drawn criticism from a Borussia Dortmund fan club, reopening debate over faith, inclusion and religious messaging in football.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Why electrification is the climate game changer we need</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8cede6bf2b4894e6745a515b8505919b8b5d3031b2cc25334785cbadff5623d6</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T08:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-electrification-is-the-climate-game-changer-we-need/a-79615979--0dbca6445640.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-electrification-is-the-climate-game-changer-we-need/a-79615979?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">From EVs and electric buses on the road, heat pumps warming homes and solar panels powering appliances, the shift to electrifying tech is already in full swing. But what exactly does "electrification" mean?</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Will Australia push for fossil fuel exit at UN talks?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dd8e67dd000aa4476b1751f009c2154feec11020adaecfa373fde55e2b38cf3c</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T07:43:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/will-australia-push-for-fossil-fuel-exit-at-un-talks/a-79782066--e866c53d355a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/will-australia-push-for-fossil-fuel-exit-at-un-talks/a-79782066?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The heat is on Australia as chief negotiator at the COP31 UN climate conference to forge a path away from coal and gas, and to protect Pacific neighbors facing rising sea levels.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Why malnutrition can go unnoticed, and what that means for our health</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:289e347ffd05bf0f96cc5338cc60aedbb18fccf5894845eb2f35769ebea8a417</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T05:48:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-malnutrition-can-go-unnoticed-and-what-that-means-for-our-health/a-79871016--a7247c0af1e5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-malnutrition-can-go-unnoticed-and-what-that-means-for-our-health/a-79871016?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">More than 2 billion people worldwide suffer from nutrient deficiencies, most of them in the Global South. The health consequences can be devastating.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>Iran war oil shock drives dip in global emissions, study shows</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:595ce7e3f11005c14da7419966a94e51722805c317a717d128306f9b2d7947eb</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T03:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-war-oil-shock-drives-dip-in-global-emissions-study-shows/a-79905937--fec20d5dba18.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-war-oil-shock-drives-dip-in-global-emissions-study-shows/a-79905937?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Global carbon emissions are expected to fall slightly in 2026, but not because of major progress on climate action. Instead, it's high energy prices following the US attack on Iran that's driving the trend.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Norway's ice hockey team says Russia replacing it at World Juniors</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a039c2928504087300fe2c2066c1425ba1deed72c91fb893bbfab81bfc988232</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T16:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/norway-s-ice-hockey-team-says-russia-replacing-it-at-world-juniors/a-79901844--43300d3ba1be.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/norway-s-ice-hockey-team-says-russia-replacing-it-at-world-juniors/a-79901844?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The wrangling over Russia's return to international ice hockey continues, with Norway saying it has been kicked out of the next major tournament to accommodate Russia. Switzerland has joined a "boycott."</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>37 years after fall of Berlin Wall: How divided are Germans?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9434f4307d8eb2af8f868acd63caceb3ca8f2ae52561154db7aff03288b7f0fc</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T13:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/37-years-after-fall-of-berlin-wall-how-divided-are-germans/a-79877461--471b79fce1fe.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/37-years-after-fall-of-berlin-wall-how-divided-are-germans/a-79877461?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Three artists share their thoughts on the reunification of East and West Germany. How do they perceive a shared "we" and what gives them cause for optimism?</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Why Nvidia CEO's affair with alleged Chinese spy matters for AI race</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6a3c542873ed49846d92e0387fff76dc7400886487e038719bcf53ff547a3a0c</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T11:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-nvidia-ceo-s-affair-with-alleged-chinese-spy-matters-for-ai-race/a-79898338--07d9155781b8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-nvidia-ceo-s-affair-with-alleged-chinese-spy-matters-for-ai-race/a-79898338?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang has apologized for an affair with a woman the US b